@startuml
title Quotas ResourceQuota - Scenario Scale Up

participant Admin
participant "kubectl" as kubectl
participant "Deployment\nController" as deployment
participant "Admission\nController" as admission
database "ResourceQuota\nhard:\n  pods: 4\n  requests.cpu: 1\n  requests.memory: 1Gi" as quota
participant Kubelet

== Etat Initial: 2 replicas ==

Admin -> kubectl : Initial deploy\n--replicas=2
kubectl -> deployment : Create Deployment
deployment -> admission : Request create pod1
admission -> quota : Check quota usage
quota --> admission : 1/4 pods\n100m/1 CPU\n128Mi/1Gi RAM\nOK
admission --> deployment : Pod1 APPROVED
deployment -> Kubelet : Schedule pod1

deployment -> admission : Request create pod2
admission -> quota : Check quota
quota --> admission : 2/4 pods OK
admission --> deployment : Pod2 APPROVED
deployment -> Kubelet : Schedule pod2

note right
  Etat actuel:
  2 pods Running
  200m CPU / 256Mi RAM utilises
end note

== Tentative Scale Up: 10 replicas ==

Admin -> kubectl : kubectl scale\n--replicas=10
kubectl -> deployment : Update desired replicas
deployment -> deployment : Need 8 more pods

deployment -> admission : Request create pod3
admission -> quota : Check: 3/4 pods
admission --> deployment : Pod3 APPROVED

deployment -> admission : Request create pod4
admission -> quota : Check: 4/4 pods\nLIMIT REACHED
admission --> deployment : Pod4 APPROVED (last one)

deployment -> admission : Request create pod5
admission -> quota : Check: would be 5/4\nEXCEEDED
quota -[#red]-> admission : QUOTA EXCEEDED
admission -[#red]-> deployment : Pod5 REJECTED

deployment -> admission : Request create pod6-10
admission -[#red]-> deployment : All REJECTED\nQuota exceeded

note right of deployment
  Event created:
  Type: Warning
  Reason: FailedCreate
  Message: exceeded quota: project-quota
end note

== Etat Final ==

Admin -> kubectl : kubectl get deployment
kubectl --> Admin : spec.replicas: 10\nstatus.replicas: 4\nstatus.readyReplicas: 4

Admin -> kubectl : kubectl get events
kubectl --> Admin : Warning FailedCreate\nexceeded quota: project-quota

note over Admin,quota
  RESULTAT:
  - Demande: 10 pods
  - Crees: 4 pods (limite quota)
  - Etat desire vs reel: mismatch OK
  - Cluster protege contre surconsommation
end note

@enduml
